-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * NVIDIA's display driver in the boot image, so the boot splash runs on an NVIDIA screen: nvidia-drm with
    nvidia-modeset, nvidia and their firmware, loaded by udev for an NVIDIA display device; modeset and fbdev on
  * SPARKY_STEREO_NVIDIA_EARLY: auto (an NVIDIA display device, or a live system), yes or no; a system that
    turned NVIDIA's driver off keeps it out of the boot image too
  * On 32-bit UEFI (EFI mixed mode) the kernel starts with nokaslr: at a randomized physical address Linux maps
    its firmware-call return trampoline without execute permission and stops at the first firmware call
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * First version: the saved choice of the main screen exported for the boot
  * GRUB at the main screen's resolution, kept through the kernel
  * The boot splash in the saved 3D mode or stereo layout (plymouth.stereo=)
  * The login screen gets the display settings (Plasma Login Manager, SDDM)
  * The splash handed over to the login screen with no new mode set
